    "notes": "Inspected all 48 final source/shared/medium-fi/native views in one continuous author/build/inspect/fix pass. Specific cross-shaped pale marble library with raised basement, paired side stairs, three open pointed portico arches/four pale shafts/dark collars and ties, a real central entrance and two recessed window rows with opaque backs and simple metal grilles. Main lead dome sits on an octagonal drum; three small portico domes and shallow lead vaults over three arms retain the roof identity. Front fountain has a geometric gold recess/crest, tap and actual recessed basin floor/lips. Closed exposed window-header ends, aligned those headers with the wall thickness, made the basin hollow and tightened its ground opening. Restored simple window rows in the skyline to avoid blank far walls. Corrected the provider control from beneath the Audience Chamber canopy into an uncovered gap without changing the model world position or any GLB; 31 pixel-identical inspected views were retained and 17 changed final views inspected. All eight earlier palace members retain their approved input/source/runtime pins. The native fixture renders this member against native context, not a combined nine-model scene."
